# Documentation Style Rule

Use when documenting classes, methods, or public APIs in MasterFabric.

## Class Documentation

```dart
/// 🚀 **MyView**
///
/// This view displays [brief description].
/// [Additional context about when and why to use it].
///
/// Features:
/// - 🔄 Auto-refresh
/// - 📊 Real-time data
/// - ❌ Error handling
///
/// {@category Views}
/// {@subCategory Home}
class MyView extends MasterViewCubit<MyCubit, MyState> {
```

## Emoji Conventions

| Emoji | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| 🚀 | Initialization, start, launch |
| ✅ | Success, done |
| ❌ | Error, failure |
| ⚠️ | Warning, caution |
| 🔍 | Debug, search, inspect |
| 📊 | Data, statistics |
| 🔄 | State change, refresh |
| 🧭 | Navigation |
| 📱 | Device, platform |
| 🌐 | Network |
| 💾 | Storage |
| 🔐 | Security, permissions |
| 🏗️ | Structure, scaffold |
| 🎯 | Purpose, target |
| 🛠️ | Helper, utility |
| 🗂️ | Config, organization |

## Parameter Documentation

```dart
/// Creates a [MyWidget].
///
/// [child] is the main content to display.
/// [padding] controls horizontal and vertical padding; defaults to 16.0.
const MyWidget({
  super.key,
  required this.child,
  this.padding = 16.0,
});
```

